{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q50980","formula":"C₅H₄N₄O₂","hill":"C5H4N4O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":4.0,"N":4.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Xanthine","ru":"Ксантин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Xanthine ( or , from Ancient Greek ξανθός xanthós 'yellow' for its yellowish-white appearance; archaically xanthic acid; systematic name 3,7-dihydropurine-2,6-dione) is a purine base found in most human body tissues and fluids, as well as in other organisms. Several stimulants are derived from xanthine, including caffeine, theophylline, and theobromine. Xanthine is a product on the pathway of purine degradation.","ru":"Ксанти́н — пуриновое основание, обнаруживаемое во всех тканях организма. Бесцветные кристаллы, хорошо растворимые в растворах щелочей и кислот, формамиде, горячем глицерине и плохо растворимые в воде, этаноле и эфире."},"fame":43,"pubchemCid":1188,"mass":152.11,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=NC2=C(N1)C(=O)NC(=O)N2","inchikey":"LRFVTYWOQMYALW-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3,7-dihydropurine-2,6-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1188","atoms":15,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.209,"y":-2.66,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.995,"y":1.053,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.717,"y":1.416,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":2.079,"y":-0.666,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.597,"y":-0.797,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":1.728,"y":1.542,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.725,"y":-0.495,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.545,"y":0.865,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.347,"y":-1.441,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.85,"y":0.597,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.639,"y":0.588,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.804,"y":2.427,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":2.579,"y":-1.546,"z":0.001,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.415,"y":-1.4,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":3.71,"y":0.733,"z":0.001,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,8,2],[1,9,2],[2,7,1],[2,9,1],[2,11,1],[3,6,1],[3,10,1],[3,12,